# SYNOPSIS

```usage
master-stack
```

# DESCRIPTION

`master-stack` places the windows of radharc(4)'s `tile` workspaces whose layout is `master-stack`, as dwm's tile does.
The first windows in the workspace's order, the masters, share a column on the left, `ratio` percent of the screen's width; the rest share the column on the right.
With no masters, or with only masters, one column has them all.
In a column, the windows divide its height evenly, and the last takes what doesn't divide.
Radharc puts a new window first in the order, so it becomes the master.

It registers with Radharc at `/svc/windows/layout` (radharc-layoutprovider(5)) and answers radharc-layout(5).
It holds no state: Radharc keeps each workspace's order and parameters, and passes them in each call, so it is restarted or replaced without losing anything.
When Radharc closes its channel it ends with a failure, and the launcher starts it again to register anew.

Its parameters are `ratio <n> masters <n>`: `ratio` from 10 to 90, 55 unless set, and `masters` from 0 to 9, 1 unless set.
Its verbs, as `act` passes them (radharc(4)'s `ctl`):

: `focus next`, `focus prev`
  Focus to the next window in the order, or the one before, around the end.
: `swap`
  The focused window and the first master trade places; the first master trades with the second.
: `grow`, `shrink`
  The master column by 5 points.
: `masters +1`, `masters -1`
  One master more or fewer.

Any other verb is refused.

Its manifest:

```text
service master-stack
program master-stack
use windows
grant windows layout
restart on-failure
```

